  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Working for social justice - research, analysis, networking and action</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The primary function of the Commission for Social Apostolate of the Jesuits in Central America is to encourage the Province and its works throughout the region to strengthen and recommit itself to working for social justice and to ensure the necessary transformation of all its social outreach activities so as to achieve this end. In particular this mission is to be accomplished through the development and diffusion of social, theological and cultural analysis and reflection, through serving as a link for cooperation at a regional level as well as farther afield, through seeking to unite &quot;macro&quot; vision and &quot;micro&quot; actions and through developing projects with and among the poor to serve as examples of an alternative vision of society. This project will ensure a level of minimum support to the coordination activities of CPAS, in addition to providing specific support to the region wide initiatives of the Province.</narrative>
  </description>
